research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/thm-tietze-extension-theorem.md-316-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/thm-tietze-extension-theorem.md:317:[L1] Urysohn's lemma, clause 1: assuming DC, if $X$ is normal and $P, Q \subseteq X$ are disjoint closed sets, there is a continuous $h : X \to [0,1]$ with $P \subseteq h^{-1}(\{0\})$, $Q \subseteq h^{-1}(\{1\})$ ([[thm-urysohn-lemma]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/thm-tietze-extension-theorem.md-318-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/thm-tietze-extension-theorem.md-319-[L2] If $A$ is closed in $X$ and $C \subseteq A$ is closed in the subspace $A$, then $C$ is closed in $X$: by [[def-subspace-topology-top]] $C = F \cap A$ for some closed $F \subseteq X$, and an intersection of two closed sets of $X$ is closed ([[def-interior-closure-boundary-top]], [[def-topological-space]]).
